## Probe: pill, invisible anchors and zoom

The demo was checked with a temporary same-origin iframe probe page (real preview at 1440 × 900 and
390 × 844) that dispatched real `PointerEvent` / `KeyboardEvent` sequences and `click()` on the zoom
segments; the probe page was removed before the commit and is not part of the deliverable. Results
(desktop and mobile identical unless noted):

```
anchorElements=0 ariaHiddenAnchorNodes=0
initial curveEndpointsOnInvisibleAnchors=true curveControls=true usedSides=right/left
zoomButtons=3 container=44x116 radius=14px outline=1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08) padding=4px
surfaceBg=true stacked=true position12=true glyphOnly=true labels=true
initialScale=1
zoomMax=1.5 atMaxDisabled=true disabledOpacity=0.4
maxIgnored=1.5
zoomMin=0.5 atMinDisabled=true
fitScale=1
dragAtZoomDelta=40/20 expectedScaleDrag=true
afterZoomDrag curveEndpointsOnInvisibleAnchors=true curveControls=true
thresholdAtZoom=true
fitAfterDrag=true bothCardsVisible=true
keyboard16=true
homeReset=true afterHome curveEndpointsOnInvisibleAnchors=true curveControls=true
clampInside=true afterClamp curveEndpointsOnInvisibleAnchors=true curveControls=true
desktop overflow=false scrollWidth=1440 clientWidth=1440
mobile  overflow=false scrollWidth=390  clientWidth=390
```

What the probe proves:

- **Invisible anchors:** there is no anchor markup at all (`.demo-anchor` /
  `.demo-card__anchors` / `[data-anchor]` count = 0), so the cards have no visible or hidden dots.
  The four side-midpoint anchor positions (4 px inside each card edge) are computed as geometry only,
  and the curved path still starts and ends exactly on the used ones — in every state: initial, after
  a drag at 150 % zoom, after keyboard steps, after `Home` and after clamping. The Bézier control
  points stay 48 px (`--space-48`) along the used sides' normals.
- **Grouped zoom pill:** one container 44 × 116 px at 12 px from the surface's bottom-left corner,
  `border-radius` 14 px (`--radius-md`), `--surface` background (`rgb(26, 29, 26)`), 1 px
  `--border` outline (`rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)`), 4 px padding, three stacked 36 px segments with
  1 px separators; glyph-only content (`+`, `−`, fit corners drawn in CSS), English `aria-label`s and
  `data-label` tooltips (no native `title`).
- **Zoom behaviour unchanged:** limits 1.5 / 0.5 with the corresponding segment disabled at 0.4
  opacity, an extra click at a limit is ignored, fit returns to 1.00 and both cards are visible again
  after dragging; at 150 % a 60/30 px screen drag moves the card 40/20 world px (`delta / scale`), the
  4 px drag threshold stays in screen pixels and keyboard steps stay one canvas-grid step (16 px) in
  world space. Threshold, pointer capture, clamping, `Home`, reduced motion and no horizontal overflow
  at both sizes are preserved.

